{
  "_readme": {
    "howToAdd": "One object in 'results' = one before/after card. Order in this array = order on the page. Copy an entry, point 'src' at the new collage and fill in the fields.",
    "images": "Every collage is a finished 1200x1200 WebP: Before on the LEFT, After on the RIGHT, lavender label bar across the top. It lives in its service folder under images/services/<service-title>/ - the same folder the service modal uses. See images/README.md.",
    "enabled": "Set \"enabled\": false to hide one result without deleting it. Keep it false until the clinical details, consent, caption and final image have all been approved.",
    "service": "Must match the service title in data/services.json character for character, so the caption matches the service page.",
    "area": "Treatment area, e.g. \"Glabella\". Shown after the service name. LEFT EMPTY ON PURPOSE - nothing is published until the clinic approves it. 'areaToConfirm' holds an editorial guess read off the image; it is never rendered. To publish one, move the approved wording into 'area' and delete 'areaToConfirm'.",
    "sessionsTiming": "Optional second caption line, e.g. sessions \"1 session\" and timing \"2 weeks after treatment\". Both are omitted unless filled in - never publish a count or a timing that has not been verified.",
    "section": "'initialRows' is how many GRID ROWS show before the visitor expands. The grid is 3 columns on desktop, 2 on tablet and 1 on mobile, so two rows means 6, 4 and 2 cards - the renderer counts the columns itself. {count} in expandLabel is replaced with the number of enabled results."
  },
